# Coding style check

Python style for this repo is `tools/coding_style.py`. After editing Python, run it from the repo root and fix what it reports before finishing:

```powershell
.venv\Scripts\python.exe tools/coding_style.py
```

Pass specific files when the change is small. The `@override` check still reads the whole tree so base classes resolve.

`@override` comes from `typing_extensions` (the project supports Python 3.11). Put it on a method that overrides a concrete in-project base method, above `@checked`. Do not add it only because the base method is `@abstractmethod` or `@required`. `__init__` and `__new__` are exempt. Do not enable mypy `explicit-override` or pyright `reportImplicitOverride`; those also flag abstract implementations.

`@required` lives in `ConnectEd.core.required`. Use it for a hook the subclass must implement when the class is not an `ABC`. The body is `...`; the decorator raises `NotImplementedError`. Put `@classmethod` above `@required`. On an `ABC`, use `@abstractmethod`.
